  "id": "jatra_bengali_theatre_song",
  "name": "Jatra (Bengali open-air theatre song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Jatra, the travelling open-air folk theatre of Bengal and Odisha, grew out of Vaishnava devotional processions and by the late nineteenth century was run by professional companies, many with offices on Chitpur Road in Kolkata. Mythological, historical and social plays are staged in the round and interspersed with songs, and a performance opens with an instrumental prelude (the 'concert') in which harmonium and tabla are joined by clarinet, cornet and violin.",
  "recipe": "classic South Asian early-1950s jatra, ballad Poetry, indian bard branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. harmonium indian, pitched indian rosewood rosewood tabla, clarinet, cornet, fiddle. kolkata dum dum EMI hmv 1928-present major-flagship kolkata hmv dum dum studio. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console. tape 15ips.",
